==Battleground==
*1 [[Ragin' Gory]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*6 [[Hackey]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*3 [[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gories]] spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*4 [[Zollow]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*2 [[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gories]] spawn after 113.33 seconds<sup>3,400f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 75% HP:
**3 [[Zollow]]s spawn, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Use [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark units]] such as [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] and [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]] to keep the Ragin' Gories in place, but don't bring [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] or [[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Wargod Nobunaga]] because Ragin' Gory is [[Immune to Freeze|immune to freeze]]. The Hackeys can destroy your base quickly, so don't let them gain too much ground. The Zollows shouldn't be that much of a problem, since they spawn infrequently. Thanks to Ragin' Gory's Behemoth type, he can easily be disposed of by
[[:Category:Behemoth Slayer Cats|Behemoth Slayers]] like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N103 (Rare Cat)|Gas Mask Cat]] and [[Adventurer Kanna (Uber Rare Cat)|Fabled Adventure Girl Kanna]].

==Trivia==
*In [[Version 11.5 Update|Version 11.5]], which added the [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] type and applied it to [[Ragin' Gory]], Gene Salesmen retroactively became the first stage to contain a Behemoth.

